{"qid":"Q42585","names":["Kingdom of Bohemia"],"title":"Kingdom of Bohemia","endonym":{"native":"Königreich Böhmen","lang":"de"},"capsule":"The Kingdom of Bohemia emerged as a formal hereditary kingdom in 1198 under Přemysl Ottokar I, who secured the Golden Bull of Sicily from Holy Roman Emperor Frederick II in 1212, guaranteeing the kingdom's sovereignty and hereditary status within the Empire. Under Přemysl Ottokar II (r. 1253–1278) and later Charles IV (r. 1346–1378) — who made Prague the imperial capital and founded Charles University in 1348 — Bohemia reached its greatest cultural and political height. The Hussite Wars of the early fifteenth century (1419–1436) convulsed the kingdom but produced a distinctive national religious tradition. Habsburg succession began in 1526 under Ferdinand I, initiating the dynasty's rule that would persist until 1918.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Bohemia's territorial boundaries are well-documented through medieval charters and imperial records; the kingdom's core lands are precisely attested while frontier zones (Silesia, Moravia, Lusatia) shifted with feudal acquisitions and losses.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Kingdom of Bohemia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Bohemia"},{"label":"Britannica: Bohemia","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Bohemia"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Charles IV, Holy Roman Emperor","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_IV,_Holy_Roman_Emperor"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Přemysl Ottokar I","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Přemysl_Ottokar_I"}],"britannica":null,"cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Kingdom of Bohemia","rulers":[{"qid":"Q312938","name":"Ottokar I of Bohemia","start":1198,"end":1230,"image":"Premek(2).jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Premek(2).jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Public domain","artist":"Unknown authorUnknown author","attributionRequired":false},"nativeName":"Ottokar I. Přemysl","nativeLang":"de"},{"qid":"Q175833","name":"Wenceslaus I of Bohemia","start":1230,"end":1253,"image":"VaclavGelnhausenovekodexu.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/VaclavGelnhausenovekodexu.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Public domain","artist":"Jan z Gelnhausenu","attributionRequired":false},"nativeName":"Wenzel I.","nativeLang":"de"},{"qid":"Q150320","name":"Ottokar II of Bohemia","start":1253,"end":1278,"image":"PecetpoII.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/PecetpoII.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Public domain","artist":"Otakarus","attributionRequired":false},"nativeName":"Ottokar II. Přemysl","nativeLang":"de"},{"qid":"Q155581","name":"Wenceslaus II of Bohemia","start":1278,"end":1305,"image":"Vaclav2 trun.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Vaclav2%20trun.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Public domain","artist":"Master of the Codex Manesse (Additional Painter I)","attributionRequired":false},"nativeName":"Wenzel II.","nativeLang":"de"},{"qid":"Q54040","name":"Wenceslaus III of Bohemia","start":1305,"end":1306,"image":"Wenzel3.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Wenzel3.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","artist":"No machine-readable author provided. Mathiasrex assumed (based on copyright claims).","attributionRequired":true},"nativeName":"Wenzel III.","nativeLang":"de"},{"qid":"Q168254","name":"Rudolf I of Bohemia","start":1306,"end":1307,"image":"Rudolph III of Habsburg.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/R